1) “The unexamined life is not worth living.” — Socrates

You can be incredibly busy and still never ask where your life is actually taking you. Sometimes moving forward begins by stopping long enough to see the direction.

{URL}

2) Socrates was not advocating endless self-doubt. His questions went deeper: Why do I live this way? Why do I make these choices? What genuinely matters to me? What should I change?

{URL}

3) When did you last honestly ask yourself: “Do I like the direction my life is taking?” Perhaps an examined life begins with exactly that kind of question.

{URL}
